node_modules/

# Proving artefacts, copied out of atrum-core by scripts/sync-assets.sh.
#
# NEVER COMMIT THESE. Every one of them is gitignored in atrum-core too, and for a
# load-bearing reason: `snarkjs zkey contribute` is deliberately non-deterministic, so a
# zkey committed here would only ever match the machine that built it. atrum-core learned
# this the expensive way by committing verification keys -- a clean `git pull` then failed a
# third of the Solidity suite with InvalidProof(), which looks exactly like broken contracts.
#
# Re-sync instead: npm run sync
public/circuits/
public/fixtures/
public/vendor/

# Harness output, written by hand when recording a run.
results/*.json

# `npm run browser-baseline` output. Describes this machine and this browser build, and is
# regenerated on every run -- the numbers worth keeping live in atrum-core's HANDOFF.md.
browser-baseline.json
